`info` and `run` take a skill folder, or a published name when a server is configured (`aip config`, or AIP_SERVER).
usage: aip run [-h] [--input INPUT] [--interactive] [--run-file RUN_FILE]
               [--threshold NAME=VALUE]
               skill_dir|name

Run a procedure, pausing when the client must decide: a skill folder runs
locally, a published name runs on the server.

positional arguments:
  skill_dir|name

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --input, -i INPUT     JSON object for the start step; `-` reads stdin
  --interactive         prompt on the terminal instead of pausing to a run
                        file
  --run-file RUN_FILE   where to write the run file on pause
  --threshold NAME=VALUE
                        override a decision threshold
usage: aip-spec <command> [args]        (AIP format 0.5a1)

commands:
  validate
  schema
  runtime
  skill
  example
  --version

Running a skill is the `aip` package: https://github.com/zach-blumenfeld/aip

